{
  "case_id": "2016-15-1503",
  "document_hash": "01b1e0b1cf378dcae284afc0a584df56fc27ae927c62a176f44a3df1c7568b54",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "John S. Williams",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1503",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "01b1e0b1cf378dcae284afc0a584df56fc27ae927c62a176f44a3df1c7568b54",
      "evidence_id": "ev-01b1e0b1cf37-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In Brady v. Maryland, this Court established the now familiar principle that the prosecution must disclose to the defense all favorable and material information. This case involves a clear violation of that principle. Here the prosecution suppressed information that a serial assaulter of women had been seen acting suspiciously at the crime scene before police arrived. The prosecution further suppressed that this man's girlfriend was in the alley at the time, yet he did not speak to her and she did not speak to him."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "John S. Williams",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1503",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "01b1e0b1cf378dcae284afc0a584df56fc27ae927c62a176f44a3df1c7568b54",
      "evidence_id": "ev-01b1e0b1cf37-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "They would have told the jury that during October 1984, in this neighborhood, this man committed similar assaults against similar victims. They would have then posited to the jury that the same person who had accosted a D.C. councilwoman in an alley and attacked her --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1503",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "01b1e0b1cf378dcae284afc0a584df56fc27ae927c62a176f44a3df1c7568b54",
      "evidence_id": "ev-01b1e0b1cf37-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: I'm sorry, but I -- I -- my greatest difficulty with Mr. McMillan is that clearly his '92 crime, which was decades after this crime, suggests a similarity that would have been very potent at a trial. But the disclosure of this Brady, of Mr. McMillan, wouldn't have led to the introduction of that later-committed crime."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1503",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "01b1e0b1cf378dcae284afc0a584df56fc27ae927c62a176f44a3df1c7568b54",
      "evidence_id": "ev-01b1e0b1cf37-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 11,
        "start": 11
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: The alternative perpetrator theory does seem completely inconsistent with the defenses that were put on at trial. I -- I'm not sure how you can say that they could have used both."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "John S. Williams",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1503",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "01b1e0b1cf378dcae284afc0a584df56fc27ae927c62a176f44a3df1c7568b54",
      "evidence_id": "ev-01b1e0b1cf37-0000-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "would be two reasons. And first, he didn't hang around for an hour. He was only at the crime scene for approximately five minutes according to --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Rice",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1503",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "01b1e0b1cf378dcae284afc0a584df56fc27ae927c62a176f44a3df1c7568b54",
      "evidence_id": "ev-01b1e0b1cf37-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In this incredibly close case the government not only wrongfully suppressed evidence of two alternative perpetrators, but also withheld critical impeachment evidence concerning a key witness against Overton Carrie Eleby."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Rice",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1503",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "01b1e0b1cf378dcae284afc0a584df56fc27ae927c62a176f44a3df1c7568b54",
      "evidence_id": "ev-01b1e0b1cf37-0001-0003",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the government didn't turn over this piece of impeachment evidence about her having persuaded another witness to lie in the investigation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Dreeben",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1503",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "01b1e0b1cf378dcae284afc0a584df56fc27ae927c62a176f44a3df1c7568b54",
      "evidence_id": "ev-01b1e0b1cf37-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "This Court can have confidence in the integrity of these verdicts. The evidence of a group attack was strong and was corroborated by multiple sources who personally witnessed the planning, carrying out, and culmination of the attack."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1503",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "01b1e0b1cf378dcae284afc0a584df56fc27ae927c62a176f44a3df1c7568b54",
      "evidence_id": "ev-01b1e0b1cf37-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Mr. Dreeben, can I ask about the facts of this? And it's a -- it's a similar question on the other side to the one Justice Alito"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1503",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "01b1e0b1cf378dcae284afc0a584df56fc27ae927c62a176f44a3df1c7568b54",
      "evidence_id": "ev-01b1e0b1cf37-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. DREEBEN: So first of all, Justice Kagan, the government looked as hard as it could for witnesses. Not all of the buildings that back up on this alley are residential buildings. There's a bank. It doesn't have windows. There's brick walls."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1503",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "01b1e0b1cf378dcae284afc0a584df56fc27ae927c62a176f44a3df1c7568b54",
      "evidence_id": "ev-01b1e0b1cf37-0002-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The way that the government actually found out that a group attack occurred was because a woman anonymously approached a police officer on the night of the crime and said she he saw Clifton Yarborough standing by the alley on 9th Street, turning his head back and forth like a lookout."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1503",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "01b1e0b1cf378dcae284afc0a584df56fc27ae927c62a176f44a3df1c7568b54",
      "evidence_id": "ev-01b1e0b1cf37-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So I think the community here was basically under siege. This was a crisis. And witnesses don't come forward necessarily when they may have fear about it or they just don't want to get involved."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1503",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "01b1e0b1cf378dcae284afc0a584df56fc27ae927c62a176f44a3df1c7568b54",
      "evidence_id": "ev-01b1e0b1cf37-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: Is -- was the judge -- the superior court judge who decided the post-trial motions, the Brady motion, the same judge as the judge who presided over --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1503",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "01b1e0b1cf378dcae284afc0a584df56fc27ae927c62a176f44a3df1c7568b54",
      "evidence_id": "ev-01b1e0b1cf37-0002-0005",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "videotape of Alston's statement to the police in late November. Look at the videotape of Bennett's statement to the police in February."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1503",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "01b1e0b1cf378dcae284afc0a584df56fc27ae927c62a176f44a3df1c7568b54",
      "evidence_id": "ev-01b1e0b1cf37-0002-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 43
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: What about the attack that Mr. Williams described? The McMillan's attack on the council woman."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1503",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "01b1e0b1cf378dcae284afc0a584df56fc27ae927c62a176f44a3df1c7568b54",
      "evidence_id": "ev-01b1e0b1cf37-0002-0007",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. DREEBEN: Well, I think the crime actually quite different. Yes, there are some similarities. It's the neighborhood. He does drag somebody into the alley. But that crime, unlike this one which involved an act with a pole, that crime resulted in McMillan being convicted of murder and sodomy, sodomy defined as a crime involving use of the sexual organ to commit the act, and he was seen running away from the victim pulling up his pants."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1503",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "01b1e0b1cf378dcae284afc0a584df56fc27ae927c62a176f44a3df1c7568b54",
      "evidence_id": "ev-01b1e0b1cf37-0002-0008",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "because they had such an obvious small-group theory of the crime, Alston and Bennett; and only one of them argued it and that was Rouse."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1503",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "01b1e0b1cf378dcae284afc0a584df56fc27ae927c62a176f44a3df1c7568b54",
      "evidence_id": "ev-01b1e0b1cf37-0002-0009",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Why was his name not given to the defense?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1503",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "01b1e0b1cf378dcae284afc0a584df56fc27ae927c62a176f44a3df1c7568b54",
      "evidence_id": "ev-01b1e0b1cf37-0002-0010",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: But -- but if you had -- you had been asked you would have told the prosecutor at the time that this is not Brady material, so far as, McMillan is concerned? That's -- that's the advice you would have given the prosecutor, don't turn it over."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1503",
      "confidence": 0.0,
      "document_hash": "01b1e0b1cf378dcae284afc0a584df56fc27ae927c62a176f44a3df1c7568b54",
